--- parity notes (web source: features/admin/components/devtools/tools/HttpStatusTool.tsx + constants.ts HTTP_CODES) ---
* Composition: ToolCardContent(icon=Network, color=amber, title t('Http Status'), desc t('Http Status Desc')) wraps
  a search Input (leading Network glyph, label = t('Search Codes')) over a sortable + paginated DataTable of the
  static 19-row HTTP_CODES catalog: code Badge (sortable column) + reason phrase (BodyText) + description (Caption).
* Badge variant ternary reproduced exactly: code<300 success, <400 info, <500 warning, else danger (HttpStatusClass.forCode).
* Search filter = web iltered memo: blank query returns the catalog (same ref); else code-substring OR reason OR
  description contains the (un-trimmed, lower-cased) query. Code-column sort toggles asc/desc; other columns inert.
* Pagination matches the web DataTable default page size (25); the 19-row catalog is one page, the bar shows 'Showing 1-19 of 19'.
* States: data binds the shared HttpStatusToolViewModel (P1/S8 HttpStatusToolSource seam), NOT direct HTTP (ADR-002).
  Every state renders - loading skeleton chrome, hard error + QueryError retry, data-empty + search-empty (friendly
  EmptyState, never a blank box), content, and the stale/offline freshness chip (auto-refresh once) over cached rows.
* i18n: pagination + common labels resolve via R.string (P1/S10): translation_pagination_{first,previous,next,last,showing},
  translation_common_{noData,refresh}, translation_a11y_loading. Telemetry: view.opened {surface:'HttpStatusTool'} (P1/S11).
* a11y: search field exposes a set-text action; refresh + retry are labelled; the loading region carries a 'Loading'
  contentDescription; the Network glyph is decorative (null contentDescription).

--- known parity-faithful i18n gap (honesty: no silent drift) ---
* The six tool-specific keys the web passes to t() - 'Http Status', 'Http Status Desc', 'Search Codes', 'Status Code',
  'Status Text', 'Status Desc' - were verified ABSENT from the shared P1/S10 catalog (apps/shared/i18n/catalog/en.json)
  at authoring time, so i18next renders the key text itself. The native surface reproduces this byte-for-byte via the
  labelFor() boundary helper (identical to the sibling ClientUtilitiesSection, whose tool keys are likewise absent).
  Adding the keys requires editing the shared catalog + regenerating string resources, which is OUT OF SCOPE here
  (allowed files = the surface dir + this log; shared i18n catalog is shared infrastructure). The HTTP reason phrases
  + descriptions are domain data shipped verbatim by the web constants.ts (not i18n), carried as-is for parity.

